## Backdoor found in widely used Linux utility targets encrypted SSH connections
<https://arstechnica.com/security/2024/03/backdoor-found-in-widely-used-linux-utility-breaks-encrypted-ssh-connections/>
_Ars Technica · by Dan Goodin · published 2024-03-29_
_fetched via http · ~1214 tokens · retrieved 2026-11-25T14:00:00Z_

Researchers have found a malicious backdoor in a compression tool that made its way into widely used Linux distributions, including those from Red Hat and Debian.

The compression utility, known as [xz Utils](https://github.com/tukaani-project/xz), introduced the malicious code in versions 5.6.0 and 5.6.1, [according to](https://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2024/03/29/4) Andres Freund, the developer who discovered it.

